---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { pageGraph, webPage, siteUrl } from '../lib/seo';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import AnchorHeading from '../components/AnchorHeading.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import { appEntries, researchEntries } from '../lib/content';
const apps = appEntries().length;
const research = researchEntries().length;
const jsonLd = pageGraph(
  webPage({
    type: 'AboutPage',
    name: 'About hideouts',
    path: '/about/',
    description:
      'hideouts is an independent lab building open-source macOS and iOS privacy and security tools and publishing evidence-first research.',
    extra: {
      about: { '@id': siteUrl('/#organization') },
      mainEntity: { '@id': siteUrl('/#organization') },
    },
  }),
  [{ name: 'About', path: '/about/' }],
);
---

<Base
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
  title="About"
  description="hideouts is an independent lab building open-source macOS and iOS privacy and security tools and publishing evidence-first research."
>
  <PageHeader
    eyebrow="About"
    title="An independent lab for Apple privacy and security"
    lead={`hideouts builds open-source tools for looking inside macOS and iOS, and publishes the research that comes out of using them: ${apps} apps and ${research} investigations so far.`}
  />
  <div class="container-x pt-12">
    <div class="prose-readme max-w-[46rem]">
      <AnchorHeading id="method">Method</AnchorHeading>
      <p>Everything here follows the same rules, in the software and in the write-ups:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Observe before changing.</strong> Tools default to read-only. Anything that changes a Mac or a device
          is a separate, labeled, confirmed action.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Separate observation from interpretation.</strong> Reports distinguish what an artifact directly shows
          from what it might mean, and say what a result does <em>not</em> establish.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Keep evidence verifiable.</strong> Outputs are hashed, screenshots are sanitized, and the original
          artifacts are published next to the analysis whenever that’s safe.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Stay local.</strong> No accounts, telemetry, or cloud uploads. Your data stays on your machine.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Be honest about limits.</strong> Every project documents its scope and the protections it does not
          bypass.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <AnchorHeading id="responsible-use">Responsible use</AnchorHeading>
      <p>
        These tools are for inspecting systems you own or are authorized to examine: your own Mac, your own iPhone, or a
        device you have written permission to test. They do not jailbreak devices, bypass passcodes, defeat code
        signing, or break Apple’s security boundaries, and they shouldn’t be used to access anyone else’s data.
      </p>
      <p>
        Research findings are published to help people understand and defend their own devices. Where an investigation
        touches a third party’s infrastructure, it reports what was observed and avoids speculation about intent.
      </p>

      <AnchorHeading id="independence">Independence</AnchorHeading>
      <p>
        hideouts is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by Apple Inc. Apple, macOS, iOS, iPhone, iPad, and
        Mac are trademarks of Apple Inc. Findings about Apple software describe specific builds and may not hold for
        others.
      </p>

      <AnchorHeading id="contribute">Contribute</AnchorHeading>
      <p>
        All projects are open source. Issues, reproducible bug reports, and focused pull requests are welcome; the{' '}
        <a href="/contribute/">contribution guide</a> lists where to go for each project. For security problems, please
        follow the <a href="/security/">disclosure process</a> instead of opening a public issue.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="mt-12 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
      <a href="/apps/" class="btn btn-primary">
        Browse apps <Icon name="arrow-right" size={16} />
      </a>
      <a href="/research/" class="btn btn-ghost">
        Read research
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
